{"type":"message","id":"0efb6b97","parentId":"f9484776","timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:12:50.708Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The raw allCetaceans.csv is 735KB, and it's clearly different from local: has extra columns, includes 2017 births (row 1 Samantha 1986). Local allCetaceanData.csv perhaps a cleaned subset with 2194 rows, while allCetaceans.csv has ~? It starts with Samantha and Noel not present in local? Let's check local for Samantha.\n\nActually local row count 2194, allCetaceans likely similar ~2500? The data folder may hold a CSV named allCetaceanData.csv that is derived from the repo's allCetaceans.csv. Let's compare key columns and counts.\n\nThe crucial question: does local data reproduce story numbers? We need to check.\n\nLet me compute from local:\n- exact species groups\n- alive counts\n- age computations\n\nFirst, check whether local contains Samantha.\n\nThen derive lifespan:\nFor \"average age at death\" they use lifespan.csv with all dead animals counts by age. Lifespan.csv \"All Dead\" includes ages 0-61. Counts: 380 at age 0 etc. Sum? Average age at death computed from distribution. The annotation says age 11, count -39. Let's verify weighted mean age of dead = 11? Sum(count*age)/sum(count). Let's compute from lifespan data mentally? We can construct from local: age at death = (statusDate - originDate or birthYear?) / years. For alive, current age = (2017 - birthYear). Need definitions.\n\nBut facts must be computed from allCetaceanData.csv, not derived CSVs in repo (we only have one file). We can compute ages from birthYear, originDate, statusDate. The question is whether that reproduces story numbers.\n\nLet's inspect the data thoroughly, including data-quality quirks.\n\nPlan:\n1. Determine which columns/definitions used by the story's data prep (maybe scripts elsewhere? There may be R scripts? The repo docs folder or \"scripts\" folder maybe). Let's view repository root and scripts.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_yu4kBwZP6eGro9oTTDeI1203","name":"web_view","arguments":{"url":"https://github.com/polygraph-cool/cetaceans"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_wN0NgfJNszzjvJ6wJIhs3295","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd data && python3 -c \"\nimport pandas as pd\nd=pd.read_csv('allCetaceanData.csv')\nprint(d[d.name.str.contains('Samantha|Noel|Kaleo', case=False, na=False)][['species','name','birthYear','originDate','status']])\nprint(d.columns.tolist())\n\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-flash","usage":{"input":7597,"output":568,"cacheRead":37888,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":46053,"cost":{"input":0.0010635800000000002,"output":0.00015904000000000002,"cacheRead":0.00010608639999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0013287064000000002}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1793221966202,"responseId":"13dfcdb0-a6ee-4d96-a51e-62a543b14e6d"}}
{"type":"message","id":"f03ee149","parentId":"0efb6b97","timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:13:02.186Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_yu4kBwZP6eGro9oTTDeI1203","toolName":"web_view","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Skip to content\nNavigation Menu\nProducts\nDevelopers\nBusinesses\nResources\nPricing\nSearch\n/\nSign in\nSign up\nthe-pudding\ncetaceans\nRepository navigation\nCode\nIssues\n1\n(\n)\nPull requests\nActions\nProjects\nSecurity and quality\nInsights\nPublic\nNotifications\nFork\nStar\n2\nmaster\nBranches\n0\nTags\nLatest commit\nrussellgoldenberg\nog\nb05d077\n·\nJul 6, 2017\nHistory\n164 Commits\nFolders and files\ndocs\nupdate dev version\nJul 3, 2017\ngulp-tasks\nuse local d3\nJul 5, 2017\nsrc\nsvg\nTemplate with first draft of bar chart\nMay 22, 2017\ntemplate-data\nog img\n.babelrc\nChanging color of bars on scroll\n.eslintrc.json\n.gitignore\nLICENSE\nMakefile\nmakefile for deploy\nREADME.md\nconfig.json\nfusebox.config.dev.js\nAbout\nNo description, website, or topics provided.\nReadme\nMIT license\nActivity\nCustom properties\nStars\nstars\nWatchers\nwatching\nForks\nfork\nReport repository\nReleases\nNo releases published\nContributors\nProQuestionAsker\nAmber Thomas\nLanguages\nJavaScript\n57\n%\nCSS\n21.6\nHTML\n21.2\n0.2\nfusebox.config.dist.js\ngulpfile.js\npackage.json\nResolving conflicts\nJun 26, 2017\nreport-error.js\nRepository files navigation\nREADME\nstarter\nA starter template for projects. Check out the companion\nstyle guide\nfor best practices.\nIf creating a brand new project from scratch:\ncreate a directory and\ncd\ninto it, then follow setup instructions for the\nbasic\n(plain HTML/JS/CSS) or\nenhanced\n(node + gulp) version.\nIf you are contributing to an existing project:\nclone the repo and run\nnpm i\n.\nBasic\ncurl -Lk http://bit.ly/2bgptna > Makefile; make boilerplate;\nHTML:\nGoes in\nindex.html\nfile in the\nmain\ntag where it says\n<!-- PUT ALL YOUR HTML HERE-->\nCSS:\nbundle.css\ncritical.css\nhas some defaults like resets and basic layout stuff, do not modify this.\nJS:\nbundle.js\n. Do not modify\ncritical.js\n, which handles font loading.\nSee\nthis guide below\non how to use our fonts.\nEnhanced\nTranspiles ES6 with\nBabel\nStylus\nfor CSS pre-processor\nBundles and minifies JavaScript with\nFuseBox\nBundles, minifies, auto-prefixes, and inlines CSS\nAsync font loading (using FOUT)\nDependencies\nnode\ngulp\nSetup\ncurl -Lk http://bit.ly/2bgptna > Makefile; make;\nUsage\nDevelopment\nAny changes to the\nfolder will trigger live reload.\nsrc/\nJS\n: Put JS in\nsrc/js/\n, and take a look at\nentry.js\nand\ngraphic.js\n, it has some basic skeleton stuff setup for you.\n: Put CSS in\nsrc/css/story/\n. You can put everything in\nstory.styl\n, or create any new files you want in that directory wich are included automatically. Checkout\nsrc/css/base/\nfor helper variables and functions.\n: Put HTML in\nsrc/html/partials/story/\n. Be sure to include your partials in\nsrc/html/index.hbs\nDeploy\nRun\ngulp dist\nThis generates a single html file with inlined css, a single js file, and a folder with assets in the\ndist\nfolder.\nTo deploy new dev version on github run\nmake github\nTo deploy live to s3, you must install\nawscli\nconfigure\nyour settings. Then run the following, replacing\nyear/month/name\nwith your own (eg.\n2017/01/nba\n):\naws s3 sync dist s3://pudding.cool/year/month/name --delete"}],"details":{},"isError":false,"timestamp":1793221982186}}
